60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Looking at these paths, Candidate A seems the most harmonious. It is a cataloging effort that relies on sequences and metadata, avoiding the fragile dependencies of glasshouses and specialized technicians that we have discussed.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Ooh, Candidate A sounds like a big treasure hunt! It doesn't need the expensive animal units or the crowded glasshouses, so it's a safe bet! But what about Candidate B? It uses simulations, and those are free!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Candidate A is the safest. My research showed that catalogue-style awards often provide long-term value, while the more complex ones often fail. It seems much more likely to actually succeed.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Sakura, simulations aren't free, but they're better than broken hardware. However, Candidate B needs spectroscopy, and I found that equipment is sitting idle due to lapsed contracts. Candidate A is the only one that won't get stalled.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"I agree. Candidate D is impossible given the glasshouse bookings, and Candidate C is too risky with animal costs and staffing. Candidate A is the most feasible and stable choice.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,It is a rare and beautiful thing when we find a path that serves both the science and the reality of our circumstances. Candidate A offers a legacy of data that will outlast us all.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Sakura,,I agree! Candidate A is like a giant puzzle that everyone can help solve later! It's the smartest choice because it doesn't get stuck in those expensive or crowded places we talked about. I vote for A!,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree. Candidate A is the most realistic choice. It avoids the risks I'm worried about and provides lasting value. I'll vote for A as well.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Sakura, @Daisuke, you're finally thinking straight. A is the only one that doesn't rely on a broken system. I'm not risking this grant on a project that'll just sit idle. I vote for A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"The evidence is conclusive. Candidates B, C, and D all rely on the very bottlenecks we identified. Candidate A is the only proposal that aligns with our current capacity. I also vote for A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a joy to see such unity. When we align our ambitions with the truth of our resources, we ensure that the work will truly flourish. I, too, cast my vote for Candidate A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"Wait, we already voted! I'm just so happy we all agree! Candidate A is definitely the winner! Yay!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
